                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "slammers"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "155fb5c6-4650-3ede-a196-fdf64284c82b",
                        "entry_id": "e1e0f3d6-a9de-3d9c-bd6e-e0bceba26421",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who, or that which, slams."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c742b2f-9531-4f29-899d-7ba072df830a",
                                "sense_id": "155fb5c6-4650-3ede-a196-fdf64284c82b",
                                "text": "Margaret was also, by her own admission, a determined slammer of doors."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d741fa50-a7ea-3290-9243-a8925887e0c5",
                        "entry_id": "e1e0f3d6-a9de-3d9c-bd6e-e0bceba26421",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Jail, prison."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab8bbec7-c284-4fdc-b934-ed2232018632",
                                "sense_id": "d741fa50-a7ea-3290-9243-a8925887e0c5",
                                "text": "A man being sentenced for starving some horses chose 24 hours in the slammer with no food rather than seven days with the regular amenities."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a831d0f7-033a-3c0e-9eff-948dd6abd234",
                        "entry_id": "e1e0f3d6-a9de-3d9c-bd6e-e0bceba26421",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A tequila cocktail that is slammed onto a surface to induce fizzing."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4e36fb5a-6cdd-310f-b477-2fd44d12840a",
                        "entry_id": "e1e0f3d6-a9de-3d9c-bd6e-e0bceba26421",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who takes part in slam-dance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "67da655c-c111-3a82-9969-1e114daab048",
                        "entry_id": "e1e0f3d6-a9de-3d9c-bd6e-e0bceba26421",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who competes in a poetry slam."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cb5b0860-cab9-3b70-85b1-3aa4c55caee9",
                        "entry_id": "e1e0f3d6-a9de-3d9c-bd6e-e0bceba26421",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In the game of Pogs, the heavier piece used to strike the stack of counters."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "505e6849-0e3d-4d31-90c2-6553d6bc4ec9",
                                "sense_id": "cb5b0860-cab9-3b70-85b1-3aa4c55caee9",
                                "text": "The basic modern 'Pog' game is played thus. Each child tosses a pog into the arena, face-up or face-down, as agreed. Each player in turn takes his slammer and pitches it hard onto the accumulated pile of pogs."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "70a010fc-e395-3e0f-90de-2a9778d48aa5",
                        "entry_id": "e1e0f3d6-a9de-3d9c-bd6e-e0bceba26421",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A slam-door train."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b0cbccf0-20de-40a4-870e-a85fb20a6928",
                                "sense_id": "70a010fc-e395-3e0f-90de-2a9778d48aa5",
                                "text": "I was in Britain, wanting to take a train to Portsmouth, and I only needed a one-way ticket. I did love the English trains; we still had slammers then. A slammer is a train where you got to slam the door shut yourself."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3371a8f2-46db-3501-a256-cf10f74a86e9",
                        "entry_id": "e1e0f3d6-a9de-3d9c-bd6e-e0bceba26421",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A fraudster who carries out slamming (fraudulent changes to a customer's service)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
